# Playnite extension CI and packaging

## GitHub Actions

- Build **Playnite WPF** plugins on **`windows-latest`** (not Ubuntu-only) so **`Microsoft.NET.Sdk.WindowsDesktop`** / WPF resolve correctly.
- Use a supported **`setup-dotnet`** SDK (e.g. 8.x) to build **`net462`** projects.

## Build vs release artifacts

- Extension profiles live in **`src/extensions.json`**. Prefer script calls with **`-Extension <key>`**.
- **Validation** (`scripts/validate-extension.ps1 -Extension <key>`): checks AddonId, versions, optional installer URL fields (if present), expected PackageUrl, and build output when requested.
- **Themes** (`"kind": "theme"`): no `dotnet`. **`scripts/build-theme.ps1 -Extension <key>`** composes kit overlay + rendered `Constants.xaml` + theme overrides into **`artifacts/builds/<key>/`** and runs the static theme checks; `build-plugin.ps1` forwards to it. Packaging produces a **`.pthm`** and a zip of the whole build drop. CI validates and composes themes instead of restoring/building a project. Details: **`playnite-themes.mdc`**.
- **Build** (`scripts/build-plugin.ps1 -Extension <key>`): `dotnet build` and a **build drop** under **`artifacts/builds/<key>/`** (copy of **`bin/<Configuration>/net462/`**; the folder is cleared and repopulated each run). No Toolbox, no **`artifacts/releases/`**.
- **Release packaging** (`scripts/package-release.ps1 -Extension <key>`): optional **`-VerifyInstaller`** (Toolbox **`verify installer`** on the extension's installer manifest), then a **release drop** under **`artifacts/releases/<key>/`** with a release zip (**`extension.yaml`** + primary **`.dll`**) and a Toolbox-generated **`.pext`**. Requires existing build output; does not compile.
- **One-shot local / package workflow:** **`scripts/build-artifacts.ps1 -Extension <key> -VerifyInstaller`** runs validation, optional verify, build, and package. Package-only builds may allow the expected `PackageUrl` before the release asset is uploaded; use **`-StrictInstallerVerification`** after publishing.
- Before publishing, run **Toolbox manifest verification** and fail on errors. Scripts resolve **`Toolbox.exe`** via **`Get-PlayniteToolboxExe`** (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Playnite`, Program Files, `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Playnite`, PATH, or **`$env:TOOLBOX_EXE`** / **`-ToolboxExe`**); they download Playnite only if none match.
  - Prefer **`.\scripts\package-release.ps1 -Extension <key> -VerifyOnly`**
  - Manual: **`& "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Playnite\Toolbox.exe" verify installer src/<PluginName>/info/InstallerManifest.yaml`**
- **`InstallerManifest.yaml`** lives under **`src/<PluginName>/info/`**. In this monorepo it is **minimal** (**`AddonId`** + **`Packages`** only, Apollo-style); **`InstallerManifestUrl`** / **`SourceUrl`** are **not** duplicated there. **`danitesler_<key>.yaml`** still carries **`InstallerManifestUrl`** / **`SourceUrl`** / **`IconUrl`** with raw GitHub paths from **`src/extensions.json`**.

